{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774113653,"nonce":"Kt7VkTCohysGiXdqHOX8rtxnc6M=","title":"Convention-configuration linkage: cross-reference presets with Mandible settings","message":"Conventions in presets should be able to programmatically link to Mandible configuration. For example:\n\n- The \"protected branch\" convention references a setting that already exists in Mandible (Projects tab). Adding the convention should prompt the user to configure the setting if not already set, and vice versa.\n- Some conventions imply required Mandible behaviors (e.g., auth requests require a protected branch to be defined). If you try to use one without the other, Mandible should warn: \"This convention requires [X] which is not configured.\"\n- Conventions become part of a configuration system — not just text instructions for agents, but active configuration that influences Mandible behavior.\n\nThis means presets evolve from \"text the agent reads\" to \"configuration that Mandible enforces.\" The convention-to-setting mapping could be declarative (convention nodes tagged with setting references) or discovered (Mandible scans convention content for known patterns).\n\nThis is a pre-release requirement.","files":null}]}